.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt BUSYBOX-LOGINUTILS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm busybox-loginutils ,
.Nm add-shell ,
.Nm addgroup ,
.Nm adduser ,
.Nm chpasswd ,
.Nm cryptpw ,
.Nm delgroup ,
.Nm deluser ,
.Nm mkpasswd ,
.Nm remove-shell
.Nd BusyBox account tools
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm add-shell
.Ar SHELL ...
.Nm addgroup
.Op Fl g Ar GID
.Op Fl S
.Op Ar USER
.Ar GROUP
.Nm adduser
.Op Ar OPTIONS
.Ar USER
.Op Ar GROUP
.Nm chpasswd
.Op Fl me
.Op Fl c Ar ALG
.Op Fl R Ar DIR
.Nm cryptpw
.Op Fl P Ar FD
.Op Fl m Ar TYPE
.Op Fl S Ar SALT
.Op Ar PASSWORD
.Op Ar SALT
.Nm delgroup
.Op Ar USER
.Ar GROUP
.Nm deluser
.Op Fl -remove-home
.Ar USER
.Nm mkpasswd
.Op Fl P Ar FD
.Op Fl m Ar TYPE
.Op Fl S Ar SALT
.Op Ar PASSWORD
.Op Ar SALT
.Nm remove-shell
.Ar SHELL ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the account tools of BusyBox 1.36.1 as built for Rach2.
On os-real,
.Xr login 1 ,
.Xr su 1 ,
and
.Xr passwd 1
are set-id applets from a second BusyBox build.
The credential files are described in
.Xr passwd 5 .
There is no PAM support and no
.Pa login.defs .
.Bl -tag -width remove-shell
.It Nm add-shell
Add the specified shells to
.Pa /etc/shells .
.It Nm addgroup
Create
.Ar GROUP ,
or add
.Ar USER
to an existing group.
.It Nm adduser
Create
.Ar USER ,
or add that user to
.Ar GROUP .
.It Nm chpasswd
Read
.Ql user:password
lines from standard input and update
.Pa /etc/passwd .
.It Nm cryptpw
Print a password hash.
.It Nm delgroup
Delete
.Ar GROUP ,
or remove
.Ar USER
from that group.
.It Nm deluser
Delete
.Ar USER .
.It Nm mkpasswd
An alias for
.Nm cryptpw .
.It Nm remove-shell
Remove the specified shells from
.Pa /etc/shells .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss addgroup
.Bl -tag -width "-g GID"
.It Fl g Ar GID
Set the group ID.
.It Fl S
Create a system group.
.El
.Ss adduser
.Bl -tag -width "-s SHELL"
.It Fl h Ar DIR
Set the home directory.
.It Fl g Ar GECOS
Set the GECOS field.
.It Fl s Ar SHELL
Set the login shell.
.It Fl G Ar GRP
Set the group.
.It Fl S
Create a system user.
.It Fl D
Do not assign a password.
.It Fl H
Do not create the home directory.
.It Fl u Ar UID
Set the user ID.
.It Fl k Ar SKEL
Use
.Ar SKEL
as the skeleton directory; the default is
.Pa /etc/skel .
.El
.Ss chpasswd
.Bl -tag -width "-c ALG"
.It Fl e
Read passwords already in encrypted form.
.It Fl m
Use MD5 encryption.
.It Fl c Ar ALG
Select
.Ql des ,
.Ql md5 ,
.Ql sha256 ,
or
.Ql sha512 .
The default is
.Ql sha512 .
.It Fl R Ar DIR
Change the root directory to
.Ar DIR .
.El
.Ss cryptpw and mkpasswd
.Bl -tag -width "-S SALT"
.It Fl P Ar FD
Read the password from file descriptor
.Ar FD .
.It Fl m Ar TYPE
Select the password hash algorithm.
.It Fl S Ar SALT
Use the specified salt.
.El
.Ss deluser
.Bl -tag -width "--remove-home"
.It Fl -remove-home
Remove the home directory.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/shells
.It Pa /etc/shells
Shell list changed by
.Nm add-shell
and
.Nm remove-shell .
.It Pa /etc/skel
Default skeleton directory for
.Nm adduser .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr login 1 ,
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr su 1 ,
.Xr passwd 5
.Sh HISTORY
The applet descriptions are adapted from BusyBox 1.36.1 documentation,
